course: dictionary
lesson: 11883
title: Breakage: things broken by accident
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A breakage is something that has been broken, usually by accident. «The shop charges for breakages» means the shop asks people to pay for the things that got broken.
explain: Breakage can also mean the act of breaking, or the damage that is done. «Pack the plates carefully to stop breakage» tells you that breakage is damage that careful packing can prevent. Try the swap: "pack the plates carefully to stop damage" still makes sense, so breakage means damage from breaking.
explain: Shops and removal companies use this word a lot. «All breakages must be paid for» is a rule: if you break something by accident, you pay for it. The phrase "risk of breakage" warns that something might get broken.
fact: A breakage is something that has been broken, especially by accident.
fact: Breakage can also mean the act of breaking, or the damage done.
fact: «Breakages must be paid for» means you pay for things that get broken.
fact: In maths, breakages are often taken away: «Of 200 eggs, 12 were breakages, so 188 were sold.»
fact: "Risk of breakage" means there is a chance that something will break.
exercise: «The shop charges for breakages.» What are breakages? | Customers who pay in cash | *Things that have been broken, often by accident | Shops that sell glass | Brand new things that are shiny
exercise: «Pack the plates carefully to stop breakage.» What does breakage mean here? | A kind of cardboard box | *Damage caused by things breaking | A long journey
exercise: Of 200 eggs, 12 were breakages. How many eggs were not breakages? | 212 | 200 | *188 | 12
test: «All breakages must be paid for.» What does this rule mean? | You must break things on purpose | Nobody has to pay for anything | *If you break something by accident, you pay for it | Shops give away broken things
test: Which phrase warns that something might get broken? | *risk of breakage | must be paid for | pack carefully | sold 188
exam: «Breakages must be paid for.» Maya breaks a glass by accident. What must she do? | *Pay for the glass | Ask for a free one | Do nothing at all | Hide the glass
